About 23 years ago, I actually did work out an
algorithm to generate random levels "like" the
levels in a game called "Larn", and had C code (long
lost) to build Larn-like levels, only to find out
that the levels in Larn were canned ones designed by
hand, and just appeared in different orders for some
minimal amount of confusion.

Thus, designing levels "like" a game has, only by
looking at the levels the game displays and trying
to guess how they are made is "more than barely"
possible.

I wish I still had that code, some of those
Larn-like levels would have made great NetHack
randomly generated levels.

I do still have "TownMaze", which with lots of
parameters, builds a different kind of random
dungeon (Bard's-Tale-like), if anyone wants to steal
the code, modify it to include secret doors and
such, and embed it into NetHack, for a summer's
project.

